# .clauderc - Solana Pipkit Project Configuration

## Project
Name: solana-pipkit
Type: Rust library crate
Purpose: Pragmatic utilities for Solana development

## Structure
src/
  lib.rs              # Main library entry
  account_utils.rs    # Account management
  pda.rs              # PDA utilities
  rent_cleaner.rs     # Rent reclamation
  token_utils.rs      # SPL token operations
  error.rs            # Error types
  jupiter.rs          # Jupiter integration (feature)
  prelude.rs          # Common imports

examples/
  rent_cleaner.rs
  token_burn.rs
  jupiter_swap.rs

## Key Dependencies
solana-sdk = "1.18"
solana-client = "1.18"
spl-token = "4.0"
spl-associated-token-account = "2.3"
tokio = { version = "1.36", features = ["full"] }

## Features
default = []
anchor = ["anchor-lang", "anchor-spl"]
jupiter = ["jupiter-client"]

## Development
Build: cargo check
Test: cargo test
Examples: cargo run --example [name]
Publish: cargo publish

## MCP Integration
Use Solana MCP server for:
- Testing operations before implementing
- Debugging transactions
- Monitoring wallets
- Interactive development

## Code Standards
- No emojis in comments or variable names
- Explicit error handling with Result<T>
- Use ? operator for error propagation
- Document public APIs
- Provide runnable examples
- Follow Rust 2021 conventions

## Common Tasks

Add new utility:
1. Create module in src/
2. Export in lib.rs
3. Add to prelude if common
4. Write example in examples/
5. Update README

Test new feature:
1. Use MCP to test interactively
2. Observe transaction structure
3. Implement in Rust
4. Add error handling
5. Create example

Debug issue:
1. Get transaction signature
2. Use MCP: "Decode transaction [SIG]"
3. Identify failure point
4. Fix in Rust code
5. Test with MCP again

